# Cornell Box materials
#
# Reflectance values (Kd) are the CIE XYZ-weighted sRGB coefficients from the
# original Cornell box measurement data (Goral et al., 1984; Ward, 1994).
# Emission (Ke) is a custom MTL extension; the value represents area-weighted
# radiance in W/m^2/sr, sufficient to illuminate the box visibly.

newmtl white
Kd 0.760 0.749 0.665
Ke 0.0 0.0 0.0

newmtl red
Kd 0.630 0.065 0.050
Ke 0.0 0.0 0.0

newmtl green
Kd 0.140 0.450 0.091
Ke 0.0 0.0 0.0

newmtl light
# The light patch has no diffuse reflectance; it is a pure emitter.
Kd 0.0 0.0 0.0
# Ke: area-weighted emission. The physical value for the Cornell box light is
# approximately 3.14e4 W/sr/m^2 (Ward, 1994), reduced here to 50 W/sr/m^2 for
# numerical convenience in a single-precision solve.
# Emission raised 4x to compensate for the reduced light area (0.14x0.14 m
# vs the original 0.30x0.30 m), preserving total radiant power.
Ke 200.0 188.0 160.0

newmtl box_white
# White diffuse box interior to the Cornell box.
Kd 0.760 0.749 0.665
Ke 0.0 0.0 0.0

newmtl sphere_blue
# Blue diffuse sphere interior to the Cornell box.
Kd 0.200 0.300 0.700
Ke 0.0 0.0 0.0
